.\" Man page for hive-cortex
.TH HIVE-CORTEX 1 "January 2025" "DruidOS 0.1.0" "DruidOS Hive Stack"

.SH NAME
hive-cortex \- DruidOS Hive Stack central orchestrator daemon

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hive-cortex
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hive-cortex
is the central orchestrator daemon for the DruidOS Hive Stack. It coordinates
communication between all Hive components including nerves (observers), synapse
(AI inference), actuator (action executor), and desktop components.

The cortex runs as root and manages Unix socket connections for all components,
routing messages and maintaining system state.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Path to configuration file. Default: /etc/hive/config.toml

.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-log-level " " \fILEVEL\fR
Set log level. Values: trace, debug, info, warn, error. Default: info

.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-foreground
Run in foreground instead of daemonizing.

.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-socket " " \fIPATH\fR
Unix socket path for IPC. Default: /run/hive/cortex.sock

.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help message and exit.

.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display version information and exit.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hive/config.toml
Main configuration file.

.TP
.I /run/hive/cortex.sock
Unix socket for component connections.

.TP
.I /var/lib/hive/
Data directory for state and models.

.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload configuration file.

.TP
.B SIGTERM
Graceful shutdown.

.SH SECURITY
The cortex runs as root to manage child processes and Unix sockets. It creates
separate users (_hive-ai, _hive-sense, _hive-act) for component privilege
separation.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hive-synapse (1),
.BR hive-actuator (1),
.BR hive-shell (1),
.BR hive-term (1)

